      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting it out\" means giving yourself permission to stop fighting the feeling, even if it's just for a moment. You don't have to *fix* the grayness, you just have to stop forcing the color back in. Since the emptiness is constant, it suggests it's not something you can just talk away; it might be a signal that something deeper needs attention. If the weariness is this deep, perhaps a more direct, gentle form of external help would be a very sensible next step.",
      "source": "target",
